<%- include('../partials/head', { title: partner.name, noindex: true }) %>

<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="shell dashboard">
  <div class="dash-head">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">REFERRAL PARTNER</div>
      <h1><%= partner.name %></h1>
      <p class="dash-sub">
        <%= partnerKind(partner.kind).label %>
        <% if (partner.city) { %> &middot; <%= partner.city %><% } %>
        &middot; <span class="badge <%= partner.status %>"><%= partnerStatusLabel(partner.status) %></span>
        <% if (partner.archived_at) { %> &middot; <strong>Archived</strong><% } %>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="dash-actions">
      <a class="button small ghost" href="/admin/partners">&larr; All partners</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ---- what it has produced ----
      First, because it is the answer to the only question that decides whether
      this relationship is worth more of the owner's time. %>
  <h2 class="dash-h2">What this relationship has produced</h2>
  <div class="metrics four">
    <div><span>Leads</span><strong><%= produced.leads %></strong></div>
    <div><span>Quoted</span><strong><%= money(produced.quotedValue) %></strong></div>
    <div><span>Approved</span><strong><%= money(produced.approvedValue) %></strong></div>
    <div class="net"><span>Revenue</span><strong><%= money(produced.revenue) %></strong></div>
  </div>
  <p class="dash-note">
    Counted from leads that arrived through this partner&rsquo;s own link. <strong>Revenue</strong> is jobs actually
    marked complete &mdash; an approved quote is a promise, and a dashboard that calls it revenue lies in the
    direction everybody wants it to.
  </p>
  <p class="dash-note">
    Work they send by word of mouth, without the link, will not appear above. Record it as an
    <a class="text-link" href="/admin/opportunities#add">opportunity</a> and name them as the source, so a partner
    who rings with a job instead of forwarding a URL does not look like a partner who produced nothing.
  </p>

  <%# Work this partner told us about, link or no link. %>
  <% if (opportunities.length) { %>
    <h3 class="dash-h3">Work they told us about</h3>
    <div class="panel">
      <table class="rows">
        <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Stage</th><th class="num">Our estimate</th><th>When</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% opportunities.forEach(function(o) { %>
            <tr>
              <td><a class="text-link" href="/admin/opportunities/<%= o.id %>"><%= o.title %></a></td>
              <td data-label="Stage"><span class="badge <%= o.status %>"><%= oppStatusLabel(o.status) %></span></td>
              <td class="num" data-label="Our estimate"><%= o.est_value_cents == null ? '—' : money(o.est_value_cents) %></td>
              <td data-label="When"><%= prettyDate(o.created_at) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% }) %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <%# ---- the link ---- %>
  <h2 class="dash-h2">Their referral link</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="mono-line"><%= link %></p>
    <p class="dash-note">
      Give them this instead of the plain address. It opens the homepage exactly as normal &mdash; there is no
      partner page and nothing looks different to their customer &mdash; and every quote request that follows is
      credited here. The code is <strong><%= partner.referral_code %></strong>, which is short enough to read down
      a phone or write on the back of a card.
    </p>
    <p class="dash-note">
      The code never changes. It may already be printed on something, and a code that changed would silently stop
      crediting the work it was given for.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# ---- the draft ---- %>
  <h2 class="dash-h2">A first message, to read and edit</h2>
  <div class="panel note-panel">
    <p><strong>Why this kind of business cares:</strong> <%= draft.why %></p>
  </div>
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="kv-line"><strong>Subject:</strong> <%= draft.subject %></p>
    <%# A textarea rather than a <pre>: the point is that the owner edits it
        before it goes anywhere, and a text box invites that where a block of
        formatted text invites copying it unread. Not a form -- there is
        nothing to post it to. %>
    <label class="draft-label">
      <span>Draft</span>
      <textarea class="draft" rows="18" spellcheck="true" aria-label="Outreach draft"><%= draft.body %></textarea>
    </label>
    <p class="dash-note">
      <strong>Nothing here sends anything.</strong> There is no send button on purpose. Read it, change it so it
      sounds like you, and send it from your own mailbox to one person who has a reason to hear from you. A message
      nobody read before it went out is the one that embarrasses a local business in a market where everybody knows
      everybody &mdash; and sending the same text to thirty addresses at once is a different activity with
      different rules.
    </p>
    <p class="dash-note">
      It deliberately claims no licence, no insurance and no rating, because none of those has been verified. If
      that ever changes, change it here and in the record, not just in the email.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# ---- log a conversation ---- %>
  <h2 class="dash-h2">Log a conversation</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <form class="stack-form" method="post" action="/admin/partners/<%= partner.id %>/touch">
      <div class="two">
        <label>How
          <select name="channel">
            <% partnerChannels.forEach(function(c) { %><option value="<%= c.value %>"><%= c.label %></option><% }) %>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Which way
          <select name="direction">
            <option value="out">We contacted them</option>
            <option value="in">They contacted us</option>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <label>What happened <span class="hint">required</span>
        <textarea required name="summary" rows="3" maxlength="400"
                  placeholder="e.g. Emailed Sue. Asked to be kept on the list for sale cleanouts."></textarea>
      </label>
      <div class="two">
        <label>When
          <input type="date" name="happened_on" value="<%= today %>">
        </label>
        <label>Move to stage <span class="hint">optional</span>
          <select name="status">
            <option value="">Leave as it is</option>
            <% partnerStatuses.forEach(function(s) { %>
              <option value="<%= s.value %>"<%= partner.status === s.value ? ' selected' : '' %>><%= s.label %></option>
            <% }) %>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="two">
        <label>Next step
          <input name="next_step" maxlength="200" value="<%= partner.next_step || '' %>">
        </label>
        <label>Due <span class="hint">optional</span>
          <input type="date" name="next_step_on" min="<%= today %>" value="<%= partner.next_step_on || '' %>">
        </label>
      </div>
      <button class="button" type="submit">Log it</button>
      <small class="fineprint">
        Logging a contact against a prospect moves them to Contacted on its own.
      </small>
    </form>
  </div>

  <h2 class="dash-h2">History</h2>
  <% if (!touches.length) { %>
    <div class="panel empty">Nothing logged yet.</div>
  <% } else { %>
    <div class="panel">
      <table class="rows">
        <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>How</th><th>What happened</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% touches.forEach(function(t) { %>
            <tr>
              <td data-label="When"><%= t.happened_on || prettyDate(t.created_at) %></td>
              <td data-label="How">
                <%= partnerChannelLabel(t.channel) %>
                <small><%= t.direction === 'in' ? 'they contacted us' : 'we contacted them' %></small>
              </td>
              <td data-label="What happened"><%= t.summary %></td>
            </tr>
          <% }) %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <h2 class="dash-h2">Leads from this partner</h2>
  <% if (!leads.length) { %>
    <div class="panel empty">No lead has come through their link yet.</div>
  <% } else { %>
    <div class="panel">
      <table class="rows">
        <thead><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th class="num">Quoted</th><th>When</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% leads.forEach(function(l) { %>
            <tr>
              <td><a class="text-link" href="/admin/leads/<%= l.id %>"><%= l.work_ref %></a></td>
              <td data-label="Service"><%= l.service %></td>
              <td data-label="Status"><span class="badge <%= l.status %>"><%= prettyStatus(l.status) %></span></td>
              <td class="num" data-label="Quoted"><%= l.amount_cents == null ? '—' : money(l.amount_cents) %></td>
              <td data-label="When"><%= prettyDate(l.created_at) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% }) %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <%# ---- the record ---- %>
  <h2 class="dash-h2">Details</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <form class="stack-form" method="post" action="/admin/partners/<%= partner.id %>/edit">
      <div class="two">
        <label>Business name <span class="hint">required</span>
          <input required name="name" maxlength="120" value="<%= partner.name %>">
        </label>
        <label>Town
          <input name="city" maxlength="80" value="<%= partner.city || '' %>">
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="two">
        <label>Kind
          <select name="kind">
            <% partnerKinds.forEach(function(k) { %>
              <option value="<%= k.value %>"<%= partner.kind === k.value ? ' selected' : '' %>><%= k.label %></option>
            <% }) %>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Stage
          <select name="status">
            <% partnerStatuses.forEach(function(s) { %>
              <option value="<%= s.value %>"<%= partner.status === s.value ? ' selected' : '' %>><%= s.label %></option>
            <% }) %>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="two">
        <label>Contact name
          <input name="contact_name" maxlength="120" value="<%= partner.contact_name || '' %>">
        </label>
        <label>Phone
          <input name="phone" type="tel" maxlength="40" value="<%= partner.phone || '' %>">
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="two">
        <label>Email
          <input name="email" type="email" maxlength="200" value="<%= partner.email || '' %>">
        </label>
        <label>Their website <span class="hint">https only</span>
          <input name="website" type="url" maxlength="400" value="<%= partner.website || '' %>">
        </label>
      </div>
      <label>Where you found them
        <input name="source_url" type="url" maxlength="400" value="<%= partner.source_url || '' %>">
      </label>
      <label>How you found them
        <input name="source_note" maxlength="400" value="<%= partner.source_note || '' %>">
      </label>
      <label>Notes
        <textarea name="notes" rows="4" maxlength="400"><%= partner.notes || '' %></textarea>
      </label>
      <div class="two">
        <label>Next step
          <input name="next_step" maxlength="200" value="<%= partner.next_step || '' %>">
        </label>
        <label>Due
          <input type="date" name="next_step_on" min="<%= today %>" value="<%= partner.next_step_on || '' %>">
        </label>
      </div>
      <button class="button" type="submit">Save</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <%# Their own pages, where they exist. Opened in a new tab and with
      rel="noreferrer" so that reading a partner's website from inside the
      admin does not hand them a referrer carrying an admin URL. %>
  <% if (partner.website || partner.source_url) { %>
    <div class="panel">
      <% if (partner.website) { %>
        <p><strong>Their website:</strong>
          <a class="text-link" href="<%= partner.website %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><%= partner.website %></a>
        </p>
      <% } %>
      <% if (partner.source_url) { %>
        <p><strong>Found at:</strong>
          <a class="text-link" href="<%= partner.source_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><%= partner.source_url %></a>
        </p>
      <% } %>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="panel notice">
    <h3><%= partner.archived_at ? 'Restore' : 'Archive' %></h3>
    <p>
      <%= partner.archived_at
            ? 'This partner is archived and does not appear in the list. Restoring puts them back.'
            : 'Archiving takes them out of the list. Nothing is deleted — the history and the leads credited to their link are kept, because a referral that happened stays a fact.' %>
    </p>
    <form method="post" action="/admin/partners/<%= partner.id %>/archive" class="inline-form">
      <% if (partner.archived_at) { %><input type="hidden" name="restore" value="1"><% } %>
      <button class="button small <%= partner.archived_at ? '' : 'ghost' %>" type="submit">
        <%= partner.archived_at ? 'Restore partner' : 'Archive partner' %>
      </button>
    </form>
  </div>
</main>

<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
